WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.960
These dumplings are made
of real shrimp meat,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.150
but instead of being farmed
in water tanks or rivers,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.800
this shrimp is grown in the lab

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.433
by Singapore-based startup Shiok Meats.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.640
Globally, we are the only company

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.120
working on cell-based shrimp and crab.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.950
Since we are making this
from the actual cells

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.010
to the DNA level, the
nutrition as well as the taste

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.210
is exactly the same as
the original product.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.300
Around the world,
startups like Shiok Meats

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.680
are racing to invent
and improve alternatives

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.920
to traditional meat production,
which is often criticized

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.880
for environmental and ethical reasons.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.260
The advantages of using
cellular agriculture

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.050
to make seafood is that

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.628
you don't need to set up large-scale farms

00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:54.390
or going to the oceans
to catch these animals

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:57.460
for human consumption, so
environmentally friendly.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.430
There is very less
greenhouse gas emissions

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.990
or carbon emissions as well,
and it's animal friendly

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.690
because we don't slaughter
animals in large scale.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.260
Plant-based meats are already here.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.288
Alternative proteins
from homegrown insects

00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:13.210
are on their way.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.690
And now with advances in technology,

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:19.107
cell-based seafood could soon
be coming to a table near you.

00:01:29.784 --> 00:01:30.770
So ever since I've known,

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:33.380
I was always intrigued by the human body.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.710
So I wanted to kind of know
how the human body works,

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.400
how does digestion happen,
how does blood flow,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.230
how does the brain work and all of that,

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.723
and always imagined
myself being in biology.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.560
This passion brought Sandyha Sriram

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.240
from her home country India to Singapore

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.350
where she got a PhD degree
in Biological Science

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.680
and co-founded two other tech companies

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.343
before starting Shiok Meats in 2018.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.200
I've been a vegetarian all my life

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.090
for ethical, more environmental reasons.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:08.040
I just put my skill for
biology and my love for food

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.730
and my love for sort of
saving this environment

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.240
and doing my part in this world together

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.473
and said, why not grow
seafood using stem cells?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.400
Cultured meat is not new.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.110
In 2013, Dutch professor Mark Post

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.660
created the world's first
burger patty from cells.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.820
So far more than 60 companies
have joined this field,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.760
backed by increasing
funding from investors.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.267
And the cell-based meat
market is projected to reach

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:40.403
$140 billion in the next decade.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.030
Cultured chicken developed
by startup Eat Just

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.670
was approved for commercial
sale in Singapore last December

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.320
a first for a cultured meat product.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.140
But while many companies are
working on cultured chicken,

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.483
beef and duck meat,
Shiok focuses on seafood.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.840
So shrimp crab and lobster
alone makes about $150 billion

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.320
worth of market share in the world.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.300
And Asia is the largest
producer, consumer and exporter

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.500
of these proteins.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.130
And it's well-liked by all of us,

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.143
and we consume a lot of crustaceans.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.710
So the process of growing
cell-based meat or seafood

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.010
involves three main steps.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.500
The first step is where
you isolate the stem cells

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.980
from live animals.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.840
These are the source cells of any animal,

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.660
sort of the birth cell that
can grow into any organ.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.930
And these cells are then
put into large-scale tanks

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.250
called bioreactors, which are
pretty much like a brewery.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.520
But instead of brewing beer,
it's brewing meats and seafood.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.320
And we feed these cells
with liquid nutrients

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.790
that convert these cells into
the actual tissue, muscle fat,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:47.623
connective tissue and real
meat at the end of the day

00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:48.456
that has the same taste, nutrition

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.190
and eventually the same
texture and look as well.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.960
Compared with farmed seafood,

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.690
these cultured versions are friendlier

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.403
to animals and the planet.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.310
Shiok Meats says growing cultured seafood

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.660
is also at least six times
faster than farming them.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.440
But it's pricey.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.070
A kilogram of cultured shrimp

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:14.060
costs nearly a thousand U.S. dollars.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.060
The key reason: the
liquid nutrient solution

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.690
that helps the seafood to grow

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.910
is an expensive pharmaceutical product

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.763
used to make things like vaccines.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.800
When we started off,
the liquid nutrient mix

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.510
that we used to feed our cells

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.000
used to be pharmaceutical grade,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.710
because that was the only
thing available out there.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.150
But what we've managed to
do in two and a half years

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.890
is to swap out some of the
chemicals with plant extracts

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.060
or edible products that makes
the food more nutritious

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.690
and delicious as well.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.830
And eventually our
process will involve 100%

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.560
plant-based and edible nutrients.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.040
And we are aiming to be
at about $50 per kilogram

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.240
by the end of this year.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.490
The company also faces another hurdle-

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.710
how to make this novel lab-grown food

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.860
appealing to customers.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.110
We're looking forward to sort of breaking

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.520
the myths that are out there

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.660
and making people understand
that this is the future

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.910
and it's as safe for them as possible.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.490
And it's the same meat and seafood

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.890
that they're used to eating.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:17.840
Shiok Meats has raised

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.170
over 20 million dollars in funding

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.710
and plans to launch their products

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.520
within the next two years.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.860
Yet it might still take
years, even decades,

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.188
for cultured meat and
seafood to go mainstream,

00:05:29.188 --> 00:05:31.690
but Sandhya remains hopeful.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.930
Our mission is to feed the 10 billion

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.140
that we will be in the
next couple of decades

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.750
and the ever-growing
population after that.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.060
As a consumer, you walk into a supermarket

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.790
and you go to the frozen
aisle of meat and seafood,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.590
and you see everything from
cell-based meat and seafood

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.340
to plant-based meat and seafood

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.330
and a small section of
conventional meat and seafood.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.770
And that's sort of the vision
for the entire industry

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.223
and for Shiok Meats as well.

